---
description: Join a remote demarkus {{.Store}}, store its token in a 0600 file, register its MCP server, and bind it to this project.
---

Connect this {{.Agent}} installation to a remote demarkus {{.Store}}: a direct-QUIC {{.Store}} server, or an HTTPS demarkus-memory-broker (hosted personal {{.Store}} behind OAuth). `/memory-init` manages a local {{.Store}}; `/knowledge-join` joins an organizational knowledge system.

## Secret Boundary

A join URL's `#token=` fragment and `--token` value are secrets. Never echo one or put one in process arguments (visible via process inspection). Tokened {{.Store}}: print the exact command with `<TOKEN>` on stdin; the user runs it in their own terminal and returns only non-secret `key=value` output. Public read-only {{.Store}}: no token, join directly. If the user already pasted a token-bearing join URL, do not repeat its fragment; extract the host and write the token as `<TOKEN>`.

No host supplied: ask. Token requirements unclear: ask before proceeding. Accept `mark://host[:port]` or bare host for QUIC, or an `https://` URL for a {{.Store}} broker (see "Hosted {{.Store}}"; never pass a token with it, OAuth owns auth). An HTTPS ORGANIZATIONAL knowledge system belongs to `/knowledge-join`. `--insecure` is explicit and only for self-signed QUIC endpoints.

## Hosted {{.Store}} (https:// broker URL)

1. Validate, register the catalog row, bind the project:

   ```bash
   "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry memory-join <shell-escaped-url> --bind {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}"{{else}}<shell-escaped-absolute-project-dir>{{end}}
   ```

   Continue only on `OK` with `broker=1` and an `mcp-url=` value; on `FAIL`, surface the message and stop.

{{if eq .Harness "claude"}}2. Register the HTTP MCP server (OAuth runs in the client on first use):

   ```bash
   claude mcp add --transport http '<slug>' '<mcp-url>' --scope project
   ```
{{else if eq .Harness "cursor"}}2. Register the HTTP MCP server in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` (OAuth runs in {{.Agent}} on first use; `mcp-serve` does not apply to broker {{.Stores}}):

   ```bash
   "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry mcp --harness cursor add-http '<slug>' <shell-escaped-mcp-url>
   ```

   `<shell-escaped-mcp-url>`: exactly one POSIX-safe shell word; never wrap the raw value in literal single quotes. Check exit status: the catalog row and binding were committed in step 1, so on failure surface the exact error, report the join as partial ({{.Store}} joined and bound, MCP server not registered), give this command as the retry, and skip the confirmation. On success {{.Agent}} reloads `~/.cursor/mcp.json` itself; if `<slug>` is missing under MCP settings, toggle it there once.
{{else}}2. Register `<mcp-url>` as a streamable-HTTP MCP server through this harness's own MCP configuration (OAuth runs in the client on first use); `mcp-serve` does not apply to broker {{.Stores}}.
{{end}}
3. Confirm slug, URL, and project binding. State: no token file; the broker authenticates via OAuth; the destination gate now binds this project's {{.Store}} writes to `<slug>`.

Hosted {{.Store}}: skip the QUIC join and MCP-registration steps below, but still apply the removal guidance in the final step; a broker row uses the same {{.Stores}} catalog and project bindings.

## Join

{{if eq .Harness "claude"}}1. Check for hand-wired {{.Stores}} to adopt:

   ```bash
   bash "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/detect-manual-souls.sh"
   ```

   `MANUAL` rows: show them, offer adoption. Re-join the selected host through this command, register the managed MCP server, then run `claude mcp list` or make its first `mark_fetch` call. Remove the old entry with `claude mcp remove '<name>'` only after `<slug>` reports connected; if the live check fails, keep the old entry and surface diagnostics. User declines or `NONE`: continue.

2.{{else}}1.{{end}} Validate, store credentials, add the {{.Store}} catalog row, bind the absolute current project directory:

   ```bash
   "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry memory-join <shell-escaped-host> --bind {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}"{{else}}<shell-escaped-absolute-project-dir>{{end}}
   ```

   Tokened {{.Store}}: the user runs this variant in their terminal so the token never appears in argv:

   ```bash
   (
   printf 'Memory token: ' >&2
   trap 'stty echo; unset DEMARKUS_TOKEN' EXIT HUP INT TERM
   stty -echo || exit
   IFS= read -r DEMARKUS_TOKEN; read_status=$?
   if ! stty echo; then printf '\nFailed to restore terminal echo; retrying on exit. Run `stty echo` manually if needed.\n' >&2; exit 1; fi
   trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM; printf '\n' >&2
   [ "$read_status" -eq 0 ] || { unset DEMARKUS_TOKEN; exit "$read_status"; }
   printf '%s' "$DEMARKUS_TOKEN" | "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry memory-join <shell-escaped-host> --token-stdin --bind <shell-escaped-absolute-project-dir>
   join_status=$?; unset DEMARKUS_TOKEN; exit "$join_status"
   )
   ```

   Add `--insecure` before `--bind` only when the user explicitly selected it. Every `shell-escaped-*` placeholder: exactly one POSIX-safe shell word (embedded apostrophes included); never wrap a raw value in literal single quotes. {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}Use `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` for a public {{.Store}} executed through Bash; for the user-terminal token command, shell-escape its current absolute value rather than relying on that variable outside Claude Code.{{else}}Use the shell-escaped literal absolute project directory, not a variable a separate terminal may expand from the wrong cwd.{{end}}

   Continue only on `OK` with one valid `slug=`, `host=`, `insecure=`, and optional `token-file=` value. `FAIL`: surface the message and stop. Reachability is checked by the first MCP call; absence of an HTTP probe is not success.

{{if eq .Harness "claude"}}3.{{else}}2.{{end}} Register the MCP server without putting the token in config.

{{if eq .Harness "claude"}}   ```bash
    claude mcp add '<slug>' --scope project -- "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" mcp-serve --memory '<slug>'
   ```
{{else if eq .Harness "cursor"}}   ```bash
    "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry mcp --harness cursor add '<slug>' "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" mcp-serve --memory '<slug>'
   ```

   Writes `~/.cursor/mcp.json` (user scope). {{.Agent}} reloads it itself; if `<slug>` is missing under MCP settings, toggle it there once.

   The catalog row and binding were committed in the previous step, so check this command's exit status. On failure: surface the exact error, report the join as partial ({{.Store}} joined and bound, MCP server not registered), have the user re-run the registration command; do not report the join complete until it succeeds.
{{else if eq .Harness "pi"}}   ```bash
    "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry mcp add '<slug>' "$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" mcp-serve --memory '<slug>'
   ```

   Reconnect MCP servers through the harness or restart {{.Agent}}.

   The catalog row and binding were committed in the previous step, so check this command's exit status. On failure: surface the exact error, report the join as partial ({{.Store}} joined and bound, MCP server not registered), have the user re-run the registration command; do not report the join complete until it succeeds.
{{else}}   MCP registration is automatic from `~/.demarkus/souls` at startup. Restart {{.Agent}} so the new server loads. Do not run `registry mcp add`; this harness does not read that config.
{{end}}
{{if eq .Harness "claude"}}4.{{else}}3.{{end}} Confirm slug, host, project binding, and whether a token file is used. State: the token is injected by `demarkus-plugin mcp-serve`, not stored in MCP config.

{{if eq .Harness "claude"}}5.{{else}}4.{{end}} Explain removal; do not perform it unasked. Remove the catalog row and token file through the registry tooling, but first rebind or remove every matching row in `~/.demarkus/project-souls`; a stale binding makes the destination gate block writes to remaining {{.Stores}}.{{if eq .Harness "cursor"}} Then remove the MCP entry so {{.Agent}} stops launching the removed server: `"$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry mcp --harness cursor remove '<slug>'`, for broker and QUIC {{.Stores}} alike.{{else if eq .Harness "claude"}} Then `claude mcp remove '<slug>'` so the removed server is no longer launched.{{else if eq .Harness "pi"}} Then `"$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry mcp remove '<slug>'` so the removed server is no longer launched.{{end}}{{if or (eq .Harness "cursor") (eq .Harness "claude") (eq .Harness "pi")}} Check that removal's exit status: on failure, surface the exact error and report cleanup incomplete (catalog row and token gone, MCP entry still present) with the command as the retry.{{end}}

## Don't

- No MCP server registration after failed join output.
- Never read, echo, log, or store the token yourself.
- Not for an HTTPS organizational knowledge system; that is /knowledge-join's lane (an HTTPS {{.Store}} broker IS this command's lane).
- Never conflate local {{.Stores}}, remote {{.Stores}}, and organizational knowledge systems.
